      "content": "Neither framing is entirely accurate on its own because the establishment of the 1948 state was the immediate and direct cause of the displacement of both Jewish and Arab populations. Most displacement was the direct result of the 1948 war of independence which began only after the UN partition plan was rejected by the Arab leadership. Contemporary scholarship typically favors a dual-framed approach that acknowledges the specific causes of the \"Nakba\" for Palestinians while also noting the state's founding for Israelis. Your most balanced introduction should explicitly present the 1948 outbreak of war as the shared catalyst for both national creation and the forced migration of millions.",
